        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-11 09:03:28.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-10948 ldlm: age out idle cached write open handles",
        "message": "LU-10948 ldlm: age out idle cached write open handles\n\nA cached write open handle stays open on the MDT until its CW OPEN\nlock is cancelled, which for an idle file is the LRU age of 600s.\nUntil then the MDT would not see the close, so the file size update,\nthe changelog CLOSE record and actions taken at last close were\ndelayed by up to 10 minutes after the application closed the file.\n\nKeep unused CW OPEN locks on their own LRU list, in the order\nthe cached handles were last used.  The periodic LRU scan moves the\nlocks not used for `llite.*.opencache_max_ms` (60s by default) to the\nhead of the normal LRU list to be cancelled, so the handle is closed\nonce the file is no longer hot.  Expired locks do not make the scan\ncancel a batch of other locks, and the oldest of these locks are also\nused when the normal list is too short for an LRU cancel.  llite\npasses opencache_max_ms to each MDC namespace through LMV with\nKEY_OPEN_DENY_MAX_AGE, including MDTs added later, and\nldlm_namespace_set_open_deny_max_age() sets it.  Setting it to zero\nmoves these locks to the normal LRU list, to be left to the LRU age.\n\nAdd sanity test_441b to check that a reused write handle stays\ncached and an idle one is closed.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanityn,sanity-hsm\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I58d0d1cf2a9c477af695051aec558a52023ebbe5\n"
      },
